00:24:35.140 --> 00:24:36.300
Like that's my favorite thing

00:24:36.300 --> 00:24:37.140
to do in Pac-Man

00:24:37.140 --> 00:24:38.440
is to anticipate

00:24:38.440 --> 00:24:39.480
my next move.

00:24:39.560 --> 00:24:40.580
But of all the other things

00:24:40.580 --> 00:24:41.460
to do in Pac-Man?

00:24:41.640 --> 00:24:42.760
No, that's my favorite

00:24:42.760 --> 00:24:44.200
and so what's interesting

00:24:44.200 --> 00:24:46.000
is like in the arcade version

00:24:46.000 --> 00:24:47.040
it's very clear

00:24:47.040 --> 00:24:48.000
and I don't know if it's just because

00:24:48.000 --> 00:24:49.040
the screen's bigger

00:24:49.040 --> 00:24:50.900
or what have you but if you

00:24:51.480 --> 00:24:53.600
can only turn left or right

00:24:53.600 --> 00:24:55.740
as you're like moving up the maze, right?

00:24:55.940 --> 00:24:58.020
If you hold down

00:24:58.020 --> 00:25:00.240
like left as your option

00:25:00.240 --> 00:25:02.440
it will register that

00:25:02.440 --> 00:25:04.280
and automatically move you left

00:25:04.280 --> 00:25:05.120
even if there's nowhere

00:25:05.120 --> 00:25:06.280
to move left yet.

00:25:06.600 --> 00:25:07.800
Like when you get to the point

00:25:07.800 --> 00:25:09.140
where you can move between left and right

00:25:09.140 --> 00:25:10.120
it will register that

00:25:10.120 --> 00:25:11.120
and move you left

00:25:11.120 --> 00:25:12.500
and that's what I really like

00:25:12.500 --> 00:25:13.380
